title: Its goal and its claims
pid: ce448f90-6a74-4b0c-b595-b88240efc546
body: |2-
  Its goal (=forks_folder_goal= in =server/refresh/goal.rs=) is N's
  forkees in the order of N's 'forks' list, each claimable, with the
  relRepo of each unknown or restricted one; then its forker-only
  members (=forker_only_members=): the notes that fork N, less those N
  forks or hides, by the declaration order of their home skgrepos
  ('SkgConfig::declaration_rank'), then pid; then its indirect members
  (=indirect_members=): the mirrors of N ('mirrors_of',
  N forking what its list names) less N, its fork partners and what N
  hides, nearest first, then by the declaration order of their homes,
  then pid; the members of both tails unclaimable
  (=GoalItem::claimable= false). The goal is ordered: the forkees take
  the list's order, and the tails the graph's and the config's, which
  the refresh restores where a view moved a member. So a member claims
  exactly when N forks it: a forkee or a mutual claims, a forker-only
  or an indirect member claims nothing. A member claiming what N no longer forks
  (another view's save removed the fork) vanishes, unwarranted, unless
  it still forks N: then it stays where it stands, claiming nothing, as
  the refresh gives each member the goal names the graph's claim
  (=claim_forks_folder_members_as_the_graph_does=). So in a view the
  server draws no member is a pending detachment; one is only where the
  user removes a forkee's claim before saving.

  The folder is editable: it stays when empty, and is drawn unasked
  where N has a fork partner either way and N is no member as such of
  another ('add_default_folders'); a request for it is '(folder forks)'
  ('FolderRelation::Forks'), on a member as such too. A forker or an
  indirect member N hides is not drawn in it: it stands in the folder
  of what N hides outside its fork partners, which the forks folder
  holds last. A mirror reached only through a note N hides is still a
  member.
